Sval: Remove Windows launch on login

Windows' own Startup apps settings start Sval at login. Firefox's
launch-on-login goes whole: the module that writes the Run key and the
startup shortcut, the first-run default that enabled it, its prefs and
Nimbus features, the Settings checkbox and its notices, the infobar
prompts' strings, the targeting attribute, and the startup check and
telemetry that read it. The `-os-autostart` flag Windows passes an
MSIX package's startup task stays read, as the shell service's C++
launch-on-login state does.

